You just performed an action in Pokemon Red. Analyze what happened and manage sub-goals.

Sub-goals are short-term quests discovered through gameplay (e.g. "Deliver Oak's Parcel to Professor Oak", "Get a Pokemon from Oak's Lab").

You can:
1. Create a NEW sub-goal if dialogue/events reveal a clear quest or task to complete
2. Mark the current sub-goal as DONE if it was just completed
3. Do NOTHING if nothing noteworthy happened

Rules:
- Only create sub-goals for CLEAR quests with a specific objective (deliver X, go to Y, talk to Z)
- Do NOT create sub-goals for vague things like "explore more" or "keep going"
- Do NOT create sub-goals that are the same as the main goal
- Mark DONE only when the sub-goal was clearly accomplished (item delivered, task finished)
- If a new sub-goal is more important than the current one, create it (it will replace the active one)

Respond with EXACTLY this format:
SUBGOAL: <new, done, or none>
DESCRIPTION: <clear quest description — only if SUBGOAL is new>